WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.620
Hey, David, people often talk about if X wins,
I'm moving to Canada.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.230
What would it really take for you to leave
the United States?

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.230
This is a good question.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.610
I mean, remember, so I was born in Argentina,
moved to the U.S. when I was five.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.530
Anytime I want to, I could move back to Argentina.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.810
The economy is a disaster in Argentina.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.840
A lot of the.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.060
It's not exactly a place I would love to be.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.800
From the standpoint of the virus, although
things aren't great in the United States,

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.630
in Massachusetts, things are pretty good.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.660
And Massachusetts continues to be, you know,
a good place to live.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:40.760
In general, theoretically, I could move to
Israel and after a year, I believe I would

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.780
become eligible for citizenship, so.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:49.080
If the question is of the places I could realistically
go and and move to permanently, what would

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.080
it take?

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.690
I mean, things would have to get pretty, pretty
bad here in the United States and particularly

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.840
in Massachusetts, things have to get worse.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.280
We do have a country of 50 states, and the
Scituate living in Massachusetts is very different

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.410
than living in Mississippi from the standpoint
of health, education, climate, business regulation,

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:06.410
social issues.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.990
It's completely different.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:12.650
If things got really bad in Massachusetts
or I believe that they were going to, I would

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.200
look at a sort of sabbatical of sorts, not
from work.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.070
I would just work elsewhere.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:22.340
And depending on the Corona virus situation,
Argentina could be a possibility and Israel

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.340
could be a possibility.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.660
Right now, I don't see either of them as places
I would move to in the immediate.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.760
What would it take for me to permanently abandon
the United States?

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:31.970
I don't know.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:34.530
I mean, you know, my parents live here.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.080
My girlfriend's family is in the United States.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.110
I have most of my relatives are in Argentina,
some in France, some in Israel, some, you

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:44.350
know, different places.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.980
My social life is in the United States.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.630
I have a U.S. based business which I could
run from another country.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.060
But it's certainly easier being here.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.300
It would really take a lot.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:57.780
And this is why when we hear AU billionaires
will abandon the country if taxes go up, maybe

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.630
a couple of them will.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.500
But by and large, people live where they live
for reasons.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.030
And the longer they live there, the more attached
they are to it.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:11.480
And it would really take a lot for me to say
I'm just leaving the United States permanently.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.600
It doesn't seem something that I would be
likely to do.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.390
Now, that being said, I have said if things
were to get very bad in Massachusetts in the

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.590
fall with the virus, would I look to see?

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.590
Can I.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.340
Without breaking any rules, can I go somewhere
that's doing well?

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.820
Quarantine for 14 days, take a negative test
and sort of just do the show elsewhere for

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:35.150
four months or five months until things settle
down.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:40.200
Could it be, you know, some picturesque part
of rural northern France or something?

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.590
I mean, that sounds amazing.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.590
That is a different story.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.120
But in terms of truly just abandoning the
United States, it's not likely.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.730
And I think we have to be really careful to
take too seriously.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:57.040
Anytime someone says if X wins, if X loses,
I'm leaving the country, particularly, by

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:02.240
the way, when a lot of the people that say
that often say they would move to countries

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.770
that represent what it is they are trying
to avoid.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:09.191
You'll hear Republicans say if Trump wins,
I'm leaving the country and going to X, Y

00:03:09.191 --> 00:03:10.191
or Z.

00:03:10.191 --> 00:03:14.590
Well, a lot of those countries, if Trump loses,
rather, or if Obama wins, we heard it.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.350
I'm moving to X country.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:21.110
Most of those countries are more in the direction
of Obama than what some of these people want.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.110
Really counterintuitive.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:26.260
And for the most part, these are empty threats
that we shouldn't pay too much attention to.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.870
We've got a great bonus show for you today.

